
Longest protein selection for Laverania transcriptomes

Overview

Select a single representative (longest) protein isoform per gene from Laverania species.
The resulting protein sets used as input for OrthoFinder to infer orthologous groups across species.

Protein sequences were filtered using genome-derived annotations, retaining one protein per gene.

⸻

Purpose
	•	Remove isoform redundancy prior to orthology inference
	•	Ensure one protein per gene per species
	•	Apply a deterministic rule: 1) retain the longest protein per gene, 2) if multiple isoforms have identical length, retain the isoform appearing earliest in the FASTA file

⸻

Data resources

All input data were obtained from NCBI RefSeq / GenBank protein annotations.

For each species, the following files were used:
	•	Protein FASTA (*_protein.faa)
	•	Protein GenPept flat file (*_protein.gpff)

⸻

